WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:11.277
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:16.449
I'm not sleepy and there is
no place I'm going to

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:22.622
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:28.428
In the jingle jangle morning
I'll come following you

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:36.870
Though I know that evening's
empire has returned into sand

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.839
Vanished from my hand

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:44.511
Left me blindly here to stand
but still not sleeping

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:51.117
My weariness amazes me,
I'm branded on my feet

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.720
I have no one to meet

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:58.491
And the ancient empty street's
too dead for dreaming

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:05.231
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:10.737
I'm not sleepy and there is
no place I'm going to

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:16.643
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:22.882
In the jingle jangle morning
I'll come following you

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:32.192
Take me on a trip upon your
magic swirling ship

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.794
My senses have been stripped

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.530
My hands can't feel to grip

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.333
My toes too numb to step

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:45.138
Wait only for my boot heels
to be wandering

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:51.377
I'm ready to go anywhere,
I'm ready for to fade

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.713
Into my own parade

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:59.519
Cast your dancing spell my way,
I promise to go under it

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:05.358
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:10.196
I'm not sleepy and there is
no place I'm going to

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:16.369
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:22.709
In the jingle jangle morning
I'll come following you

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.882
Though you might hear
laughing, spinning,

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:31.684
swinging madly across the sun

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.154
It's not aimed at anyone

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.157
It's just escaping on the run

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:41.895
And but for the sky there are
no fences facing

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:48.268
And if you hear vague traces
of skipping reels of rhyme

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.904
To your tambourine in time

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:53.673
It's just a ragged clown behind

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:56.276
I wouldn't pay it any mind

00:02:56.276 --> 00:03:00.780
It's just a shadow you're
seeing that he's chasing

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:07.387
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:12.892
I'm not sleepy and there is
no place I'm going to

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:18.565
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:25.238
In the jingle jangle morning
I'll come following you

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.283
And take me disappearing

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.919
through the smoke rings
of my mind

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:15.622
Down the foggy ruins of time

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:18.524
Far past the frozen leaves

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.027
The haunted frightened trees

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.463
Out to the windy beach

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:27.800
Far from the twisted
reach of crazy sorrow

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:31.704
Yes, to dance beneath
the diamond sky

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.973
With one hand waving free

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.476
Silhouetted by the sea

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:39.145
Circled by the circus sands

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.814
With all memory and fate

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.384
Driven deep beneath the waves

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:49.122
Let me forget about today
until tomorrow

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:54.961
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:04:54.961 --> 00:05:00.233
I'm not sleepy and there is no
place I'm going to

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:05.872
Hey! Mr. Tambourine man,
play a song for me

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:12.111
In the jingle jangle morning
I'll come following you

